## 8. Important Hardware Notes

- All HC-SR04 sensors operate from the regulated 5 V rail.
- Each HC-SR04 ECHO line requires a voltage divider.
- The Raspberry Pi's GPIO inputs are not 5 V tolerant.
- The PCA9685 and BNO085 use 3.3 V logic power.
- The BNO085 uses software I²C bus 8.
- The PCA9685 uses hardware I²C bus 1.
- Ultrasonic sensors should be triggered sequentially to minimize acoustic crosstalk.
- GPIO15 (physical pin 10) is assigned to Sensor 1 TRIG and must not conflict with UART usage.
- GPIO7–GPIO11 overlap with SPI functions and must not conflict with an enabled SPI interface.
- All eight vibration motors are controlled independently through PCA9685 channels 0–7.
- The sensor and motor angular positions must remain aligned in software.
- The first four ECHO GPIO assignments account for the soldering changes made during belt construction.
